@cuichenx thanks, switched to that approach. `MODEL_CONFIG_CLASS` now defaults to `None` on `MegatronModelBridge`, and the migrated families opt in: `LlamaBridge` and `Qwen3Bridge` set `BridgeGPTModelConfig`, and `MuseGlimmerBridge` already sets its own config. The hook-override guard is removed, so unmigrated families are rejected by the existing `None` branch, and the provider deprecation warning is gated on the same attribute. Subclasses of a migrated bridge inherit the opt-in.

`test_bridge_can_explicitly_disable_model_config` is now parametrized over every registered bridge. It checks that unmigrated bridges reject `get_model_config()` and that opting in and providing a config mapping always go together. One exception: `MuseGlimmerBridge` overrides `hf_config_to_model_config()` entirely and does not read `MODEL_CONFIG_CLASS`, so the subclass-sets-None check skips it. I left that behavior unchanged.

I also removed the explicit `MODEL_CONFIG_CLASS = None` on `GLM5Bridge` and `BagelBridge` since it is now the default. I can restore those lines if you prefer them as documentation.
